# DIAGNOSTIC, Geant4 only. Is the charge-odd dose split multiple scattering?
#
# No. This macro is the answer to the question docs/RISK.md's charge-split entry was left open
# on: with ionisation the only process a pion has, the split survives essentially unchanged.
#
# The pion here carries Transportation and hIoni and NOTHING else - the seven inactivations of
# pion_emonly.mac and pion_minus_emonly.mac plus msc. `/particle/select pi- ; /particle/process/
# dump` was used to confirm every inactivation took: after these lines pi-'s process manager
# lists Transportation, msc and hIoni as Active and hBrems, hPairProd, CoulombScat, Decay,
# hadElastic, hBertiniCaptureAtRest and pi-Inelastic as InActive, so the comparison is not
# resting on a command name being right.
#
# MEASURED, 500,000 events per beam. Split is (positive - negative) / negative, throughout
# ref/b1hadron. The two rows below THIS file printed are the second one; the msc-active row is
# pion_emonly.mac and pion_minus_emonly.mac.
#
#                      pi+                  pi-                  split
#   msc active    633.446 +/- 0.668   600.831 +/- 0.636          5.43%
#   msc off       634.279 +/- 0.668   602.078 +/- 0.637          5.35%
#
# The pi- here is the second beam of a single process, so it starts from the random state the
# pi+ run left; the same configuration run on its own gave 603.024 +/- 0.636, a 5.18% split.
# The two differ by 1.1 sigma and the conclusion does not depend on which is quoted.
#
# Each charge moves by less than 0.4% when its multiple scattering is removed and the split
# moves by a tenth of itself. The same test on the muons, one beam per run: mu+ 600.681 ->
# 599.621 and mu- 575.568 -> 576.593, a split of 4.36% becoming 3.99%. G4WentzelVIModel and
# G4MuMultipleScattering are therefore EXCLUDED, and they were the named suspect.
#
# A first pass at 2,000 events had said the opposite - the split appearing to fall from 3.58%
# to 1.19% - and that reading was one sigma of a +/-1.7% measurement. The count is part of the
# test.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 1

/process/inactivate hadElastic
/process/inactivate pi+Inelastic
/process/inactivate pi-Inelastic
/process/inactivate Decay
/process/inactivate hBertiniCaptureAtRest
/process/inactivate hBrems
/process/inactivate hPairProd
/process/inactivate CoulombScat
/process/inactivate msc

/gun/energy 200 MeV
/run/printProgress 100000

/gun/particle pi+
/run/beamOn 500000

/gun/particle pi-
/run/beamOn 500000
